    "flow": {"x": 0, "y": 1820, "text": "The flow", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2740},
    "howto": {"x": 0, "y": 3020, "w": 390, "text": "Press Play on the first board. Allow the camera and it spends a beat spotting ideas. Tap the arrow (or the sim strip on the left) to move. Get the amber dot onto the white spot: the corners close in and turn green. Tap the pill top-right to fade from Guide to Hints to Quiet.", "fill": "orange"},
    "states": {"x": 470, "y": 3020, "w": 560, "text": "The boards to the right are the same screen frozen at each step. Every tip still comes from one written rule: compare where the phone points with the idea’s target, pick the first thing that’s off, say one move. Nothing scores the photo.", "fill": "gray"},
    "edges": {"x": 0, "y": 3640, "text": "Less help, and the honest states", "kind": "title1", "maxW": 2740},
    "edgesNote": {"x": 1880, "y": 3940, "w": 480, "text": "Hints and Quiet are the same screen with less help, for once someone has the eye. Not sure and Your call are the honest states: no invented tips when nothing stands out, and no scolding when someone shoots their own way.", "fill": "gray"}
